              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If your fleet depends on dependable, efficient transportation, choosing the right dry van trailers for sale can make a significant impact on your bottom line. Whether you're an owner-operator managing a small team or a fleet manager responsible for dozens of units, the right trailer is more than a purchase; it's a long-term investment in your business. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we understand how important that decision is.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Dry van trailers remain one of the most versatile and in-demand assets for trucking companies across the country, especially for businesses that haul general freight, retail goods, consumer products, and temperature-stable cargo. If it needs to stay clean, dry, and secure, a dry van delivers. Here are the essential considerations to keep in mind before investing in new or used dry van trailers, and how to determine which option will bring your fleet the best long-term ROI.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-specs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding Dry Van Trailer Specs Before You Buy",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "specs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-specs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all dry vans are built the same, and reviewing dry van trailer specs closely can save you costly mistakes down the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-specs-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Dimensions and Capacity",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Interior height clearance"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Pallet capacity"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Cargo weight limits"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Standard dry van trailers typically come in 53', though 48' options remain common in regional operations. Be sure to consider:"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Materials and Durability",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Walls: aluminum vs. composite"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Flooring: hardwood for load stability"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Roofing: translucent for visibility or aluminum for strength"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Long-haul operations require durability. Look for:"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-specs-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Choosing the wrong size can limit your load options and your profitability. Modern fleets are also increasingly integrating aerodynamic panels, skirts, and rear airflow systems. If your goal is cost efficiency, these upgrades offer a strong ROI over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/before-buying-dry-van-trailers-for-sale/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician checking a dry van trailer's rear door latch and hardware"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-purchasing-tips",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Trailer Purchasing Tips for Fleet Managers",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "purchasing-tips"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-purchasing-tips-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When comparing dry van trailers for sale, it's important to do more than compare price tags. Your investment should support your business long-term.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-purchasing-tips-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Consider Your Fleet's Primary Haul Type",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "What type of freight do we haul most often?"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Do we need specialized flooring, riveted sides, or reinforced walls?"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Before you shop, determine:"
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Think Long-Term: New vs. Used",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "New dry van trailers often come with better warranties, updated specs, and fuel-efficient features."
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Used dry van trailers can be more affordable upfront while still offering reliable performance when sourced from a trusted dealer."
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Both new and used trailers offer unique advantages:"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-purchasing-tips-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Sun State Trailers offers both options so fleet managers can choose what best fits their operational and financial needs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
