                {
                  "id": "p-roi-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A strong fleet trailer buying guide doesn't just tell you what to purchase; it explains why certain choices matter.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-roi-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type3",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Uptime and Maintenance",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Trailers with durable flooring, corrosion-resistant materials, and reinforced frames reduce downtime. Buying from a reliable brand known for high-quality construction, like Globe Trailers or Hyundai Translead, can also reduce maintenance costs down the line."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Resale Value",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Dry vans with modern specs, high-quality materials, and consistent maintenance hold value longer. Even if you plan to keep the trailer for years, resale value still matters; it's part of your long-term return on investment."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Dealer Support and Customer Care",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Fleet managers aren't just looking for equipment; they're looking for a partner they can depend on. Sun State Trailers is known for its hospitable, straightforward approach, making purchases simple and stress-free."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
